# SEO

Applies to public marketing surfaces only. Auth, dashboard, and API routes stay out of the index.

## Metadata

- Root defaults live in `app/layout.tsx` (`metadataBase`, title template, description, OG, Twitter).
- Every marketing `page.tsx` exports metadata or `generateMetadata()` via `buildMarketingMetadata()` in `lib/seo/marketing-metadata.ts`.
- Set `alternates.canonical` on every public page via `buildMarketingMetadata` (`lib/seo/marketing-metadata.ts`). English only in Phase 1 — add `hreflang` only if multilingual is commissioned.
- Auth / dashboard layouts keep `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`.

## Crawl surface

- `app/sitemap.ts` lists only indexable public URLs (`live` entries in `constants/site-nav.ts` + published content).
- `app/robots.ts` allows `/` and disallows `/dashboard`, `/api`, `/admin`, `/login`, `/signup`, and localized auth paths.
- Default social preview: `app/opengraph-image.png`. Add dynamic `opengraph-image` routes only for real dynamic public pages.

## Structured data & markup

- JSON-LD via `components/seo/json-ld.tsx` — Organization on the landing page; Article / FAQPage where the content matches.
- Exactly one `<h1>` per page; keep a sane `h2` → `h3` hierarchy.
- Meaningful images need `alt` text. Decorative images use empty `alt=""`.

## Images & URLs

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — raw img, no sizes, no alt discipline
<img src="/hero.jpg" />

// ✅ GOOD
import Image from "next/image"
<Image src="/hero.jpg" alt="Telecel Global network operations" width={1200} height={630} sizes="100vw" />
```

- Prefer readable slugs in public URLs — not raw UUIDs. When content comes from the DB, store and query a `slug` column.

## Before shipping a marketing page

- [ ] Metadata + canonical/alternates
- [ ] In sitemap (if indexable)
- [ ] One `h1`, alts on images, `next/image`
- [ ] JSON-LD if Organization / Article / FAQ applies
